//@version=6
// LIVE TEST LEVEL 2b — venue-protected fill with a TP/SL bracket. SUPERVISED ONLY.
//
// 2a proved fill -> flatten but left an UNPROTECTED window: if the process died between
// the fill and the flatten, the position sat naked. 2b closes that window with a native
// venue-side OCO bracket PRE-PLACED on the entry bar (withheld by #82b until the fill, so
// it is already in the exit book when the fill lands). MEASURED (l2b live 2026-09-15,
// #121): the SL/TP arms on the SAME BAR and SAME timestamp as the fill — #121's arm-on-fill
// wake dispatches + creates the bracket at the fill bar (entry id=214806 @1952.9 bar 502
// 14:17:00 -> dispatching EXIT tp=1956.8 sl=1948.8 -> 215286, same bar 502). No naked
// window. This SUPERSEDES the earlier "#107 ~1-bar window, ACCEPTED not fixed" verdict —
// but ONLY for a PRE-PLACED bracket. A REACTIVELY-placed exit (gated on position_size>0,
// as in l2b_entry_update) is NOT in the book at fill time, so the wake has nothing to arm
// and it lands a bar late (measured the same morning: fill bar 502 -> exit bar 503). So
// same-bar protection is a STRATEGY-AUTHORING requirement (pre-place the exit), NOT an
// engine guarantee. Once placed, the native OCO runs server-side. 2b still exercises the
// two things 2a cannot:
//
//   * exit-order PLACEMENT alongside a live position, and
//   * its CANCELLATION when we flatten — no orphan left resting.
// Every Level 3 case depends on that path, so breaking it here once beats breaking it
// eight times there.
//
// ENTRY: a BREAKOUT stop at `higherHigh2` = max(high, high[1]) — NOT a market order.
// TP/SL are derived from that TRIGGER price, never from `close`. A stop entry fills at or
// near its trigger, so a close-derived bracket inverts: measured 2026-09-11 over 275
// VN30F1M 15m bars, a close-derived TP sat BELOW the entry on 50.7% of bars (worst 0.795%
// below) and the SL landed a median 0.403% away instead of 0.200%. Trigger-derived, the
// same bars give 0.0% inverted and the SL exactly 0.200%.
//
// PROTECTION, three independent layers (outermost last):
//   1. Native OCO bracket: TP +0.2% / SL -0.2% off the TRIGGER, one server-side order
//      sharing an `oca_name`, so the venue runs one-cancels-other itself and CANNOT leave
//      a stop behind when the other side fills.
//   2. MAX 2 CANDLES: once a position has survived into a second bar, cancel every working
//      order and close it. Measured over the same 275 bars: 39 position episodes — 26
//      closed by the bracket inside one bar, 13 closed by this rule at two bars, none ever
//      longer than two. (This replaces 2a's flatten-on-sight.)
//   3. DOUBLE-CHECK at -0.3%: `strategy.cancel_all()` then `strategy.close_all()` — cancel
//      first so no resting leg can re-open exposure after the flatten. The threshold sits
//      OUTSIDE the 0.2% bracket so it only fires if the bracket did not. Its PnL% is
//      computed MANUALLY; `strategy.opentrades.profit_percent()` reads 0.0 for an OPEN
//      trade, which had made this whole layer dead code (see the note at the backstop).
//
// Other guards: 1 lot, pyramiding=0, `barstate.isrealtime` gate (warmup NEVER trades; a
// plain `dnse:` backtest places ZERO trades — that is the proof, and it is CHECKED, not
// assumed). ENTRY GATE = `strategy.opentrades == 0`: the entry (and its pre-placed bracket)
// RE-ISSUES each bar while flat so the resting conditional tracks the moving breakout and
// can fill; after a close it re-enters (repeated round-trips — supervised test, watch and
// stop after the observation you need).
//
// NOTE ON TIMING: the flatten lands on the NEXT bar, not intrabar. The DNSE v2 plugin's
// `watch_ohlcv` skips the still-forming bar and yields CLOSED bars only, so there are no
// intrabar ticks to evaluate on — `calc_on_every_tick` cannot shorten this. The bracket
// above is what protects that one-bar window.
//
// PRECONDITION: continuous session, FLAT account, operator watching, DNSE app open.
strategy("LIVE2b fill+bracket+flatten", overlay=true, pyramiding=0, initial_capital=500000000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     margin_long=18.48, margin_short=18.48,
     slippage=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=false)

var float tpLevel = na      // +0.2% off the trigger; recomputed each flat bar (chases)
var float slLevel = na      // -0.2% off the trigger; recomputed each flat bar (chases)

higherHigh2 = high > high[1] ? high : high[1]

// (1) the CHASING entry + its pre-placed native OCO bracket — LIVE bars only:
//   barstate.isrealtime      -> warmup never trades (a plain backtest places ZERO = proof).
//   strategy.opentrades == 0 -> RE-ISSUES each flat bar so the entry tracks the moving
//                               breakout and fills; the pre-placed exit "X" lets #121 arm
//                               it on the fill bar. Re-enters after a close (supervised).
if barstate.isrealtime and strategy.opentrades == 0
    tpLevel := higherHigh2 * 1.002
    slLevel := higherHigh2 * 0.998
    strategy.entry("E", strategy.long, stop=higherHigh2, comment="STOP 1-lot")

    // Instant protection — pre-placed on the entry bar so #121 arms it on the fill
    strategy.exit("X", from_entry="E", limit=tpLevel, stop=slLevel, oca_name="brk",
                  comment_profit="TP@" + str.tostring(tpLevel, format.mintick),
                  comment_loss="SL@" + str.tostring(slLevel, format.mintick))

if strategy.opentrades > 0
    // NOTE: no oca_type — Pine's strategy.exit has no such parameter (TradingView
    // rejects it with CE10120), and its legs always form a reduce group anyway.
    strategy.exit("X", from_entry="E", limit=tpLevel, stop=slLevel, oca_name="brk",
                  comment_profit="TP@" + str.tostring(tpLevel, format.mintick),
                  comment_loss="SL@" + str.tostring(slLevel, format.mintick))

// (2) DOUBLE-CHECK — outermost backstop, wider than the 0.2% bracket so it only fires if
//     the bracket did not. Cancel first: a resting leg left working could otherwise
//     re-open exposure right after close_all flattens.
DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT = -0.3
// PnL% COMPUTED MANUALLY: `strategy.opentrades.profit_percent()` reads 0.0 for an OPEN
// trade in PyneCore (and upstream) — the per-bar update loop writes `trade.profit` only,
// and every `profit_percent` assignment lives in a CLOSE path. Using it made this backstop
// DEAD CODE (measured 2026-09-11: profit went 0 -> -6 while profit_percent stayed 0.0000).
// entry_price and size ARE live on an open trade, so derive the percentage from price.
// `_bsDir` inverts it for a short — without it a losing short would report a gain.
_bsEntry = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.entry_price(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsSize  = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.size(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsDir   = _bsSize < 0 ? -1.0 : 1.0
_bsLive  = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(_bsEntry) and _bsEntry != 0.0
openPnlPct = _bsLive ? (close - _bsEntry) / _bsEntry * 100.0 * _bsDir : 0.0
if strategy.position_size != 0 and openPnlPct < DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT
    strategy.cancel_all()
    strategy.close_all(comment="DOUBLECHECK")


//Keep position max 2 candles
if strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0    
    strategy.cancel_all()
    strategy.close("E", comment="FLATTEN")

plot(strategy.position_size, "pos", display=display.data_window)
plot(tpLevel, "tp", display=display.data_window)
plot(slLevel, "sl", display=display.data_window)
